#: ../../source/export.rst:109 69ea0826d2644841b3c244f75d188e28
msgid ""
"A 16-bit fixed-point or millimetre sample is the right thing to measure "
"and the wrong thing to look at: most viewers render it as a near-black "
"frame. ``colorize = true`` writes an 8-bit ``COLORMAP_TURBO`` image "
"instead, stretched between the 5th and 95th percentile of the valid "
"samples so a handful of outliers cannot flatten the whole map, with "
"invalid pixels left black. It is a view, not a measurement: the range "
"depends on the data, so read numbers from the plain artefact. The colour "
"form needs an 8-bit container, so ``colorize`` with a ``.tif`` target is "
"rejected rather than silently writing something else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/export.rst:117 561cde4df3ac456cbc4ce34c76b41c9a
msgid ""
"The point cloud is expressed in the rectified left camera frame: x right,"
" y down, z forward, in metres. It carries geometry only — three fields "
"per point, no colour — so its size depends on the depth map and never on "
"whether the input pair happened to be colour. Because "
"``pointcloud.keep_invalid`` defaults to false, the cloud holds only "
"pixels with a valid depth; the full pixel grid can be rebuilt from the "
"disparity map plus ``fx``, ``cx``, ``cy``, ``doffs`` and ``baseline``, "
"all of which the run report records."
msgstr ""

